quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  20,99,"(Esteemed Prophet!) In this way, We relate to you the news of what happened before. Indeed, We have given you a Reminder (i.e. the Qur’an) from Our presence."
  20,100,"Whoever turns away from it shall bear a heavy burden on the Day of Resurrection,"
  20,101,remaining in it forever. What a terrible burden for them on the Day of Resurrection!
  20,102,"(It is) the Day when the Trumpet will be blown. And We shall gather the guilty on that Day (blind), with blued eyes."
  20,103,They will whisper among themselves: ‘You have stayed only for ten (days in the world).’
  20,104,We know best what they will say when the fairest of them in conduct will say: ‘You stayed (there) for no longer than a day.’
  20,105,They ask you about the mountains. So tell (them): ‘My Lord will scatter them like dust.
  20,106,"Then He will leave it (i.e. the earth) as a flat, barren land."
  20,107,"In it, You will see neither curvature nor unevenness (i.e. any valley or hill).’"
  20,108,"On that Day, they will follow the inviter. There will be no escape from following him. And all voices shall be humbled before the Most-Compassionate (Lord), and you will hear nothing but a murmur."
  20,109,"On that Day, intercession will not benefit (anyone) except the one to whom the Most-Compassionate (Lord) has granted permission and was pleased with his word."
  20,110,"He knows what is before them and what is behind them, but they do not encompass Him in knowledge."
  20,111,"All faces shall be humbled before the Ever-Living, the All-Sustaining. And surely, he who bears (the burden of) injustice will certainly fail."
  20,112,And whoever performs righteous deeds and is a believer shall fear neither injustice nor deprivation.
  20,113,"Thus, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur’an. And We have distinctly explained the warning in it, so that they may be God-conscious, or it may induce remembrance for them."
